Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: an HDR10+ video sent as Dolby Vision by
 Always is said as the player information says it

"Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision" has a third value in Hades 1.2.3,
Always, which also sends HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision to a display that
takes HDR10+. The player information then says so as a note, code
hdr10plus_as_dv, with the setting as what to do (hdr10plusmode): on such a
display the video's own HDR10+ is the more faithful picture. The tables of
Check this setup that mirror Estuary's strings had neither, so its result
said "as intended" for that video. Both are added, with the strings of
Estuary (54969, 54970).
---
 resources/lib/hades_check.py | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

